      "id": "intro-1",
      "sectionId": "intro",
      "text": "Ranger eyes ready—look far, never chase.",
      "objective": "narration",
      "objectReveal": "none"
    },
    {
      "id": "intro-2",
      "sectionId": "intro",
      "text": "A to Z brings wildlife safely into our picture space.",
      "objective": "narration",
      "objectReveal": "none"
    },
    {
      "id": "r1-A",
      "sectionId": "r1-a-d",
      "text": "Antelope—that is our A. Antelope in its place | feet, coat, ears, and tail give clues to trace",
      "targetId": "A",
      "objective": "lexical-semantic",
      "objectReveal": "line-start"
    },
    {
      "id": "r1-B",
      "sectionId": "r1-a-d",
      "text": "Spot B: Bison! Bison is hoofed wildlife; legs, hoof shape, head, and coat help identify it.",
      "targetId": "B",
      "objective": "lexical-semantic",
      "objectReveal": "line-start"
    },
    {
      "id": "r1-C",
      "sectionId": "r1-a-d",
      "text": "C brings Camel; It walks on hooves; horns, ears, neck, or coat add the next clue.",
      "targetId": "C",
      "objective": "lexical-semantic",
      "objectReveal": "line-start"
    },
    {
      "id": "r1-D",
      "sectionId": "r1-a-d",
      "text": "A clue for D: Deer. Deer is hoofed wildlife; legs, hoof shape, head, and coat help identify it.",
      "targetId": "D",
      "objective": "lexical-semantic",
      "objectReveal": "line-start"
    },
    {
      "id": "r1-E",
      "sectionId": "r1-e-h",
      "text": "across the habitat trail, here comes Elephant for E. Elephant so grand | trunk can lift and smell and understand",
      "targetId": "E",
      "objective": "lexical-semantic",
      "objectReveal": "line-start"
    },
    {
      "id": "r1-F",
      "sectionId": "r1-e-h",
      "text": "Flamingo—that is our F. It is a long-legged water bird with a bent bill adapted for filter feeding.",
      "targetId": "F",
      "objective": "lexical-semantic",
      "objectReveal": "line-start"
    },
    {
      "id": "r1-G",
      "sectionId": "r1-e-h",
      "text": "Spot G: Giraffe! Giraffe up high | long neck reaches toward the sky",
      "targetId": "G",
      "objective": "lexical-semantic",
      "objectReveal": "line-start"
    },
    {
      "id": "r1-H",
      "sectionId": "r1-e-h",
      "text": "H brings Hippo; A hippopotamus is a large semi-aquatic mammal that spends much of the day in water or mud.",
      "targetId": "H",
      "objective": "lexical-semantic",
      "objectReveal": "line-start"
    },
    {
      "id": "r1-I",
      "sectionId": "r1-i-l",
      "text": "A clue for I: Ibex. Ibex in its place | feet, coat, ears, and tail give clues to trace",
      "targetId": "I",
      "objective": "lexical-semantic",
      "objectReveal": "line-start"
    },
    {
      "id": "r1-J",
      "sectionId": "r1-i-l",
      "text": "across the habitat trail, here comes Jackal for J. It is a wild canid; muzzle, pointed ears, paws, and tail help reveal it.",
      "targetId": "J",
      "objective": "lexical-semantic",
      "objectReveal": "line-start"
    },
    {
      "id": "r1-K",
      "sectionId": "r1-i-l",
      "text": "Koala—that is our K. It is an Australian marsupial that climbs eucalyptus trees and eats mainly eucalyptus leaves.",
      "targetId": "K",
      "objective": "lexical-semantic",
      "objectReveal": "line-start"
    },
    {
      "id": "r1-L",
      "sectionId": "r1-i-l",
      "text": "Spot L: Lemur! Lemur belongs to the primate family; watch its grasping hands and body shape.",
      "targetId": "L",
      "objective": "lexical-semantic",
      "objectReveal": "line-start"
    },
    {
      "id": "chorus-r1-3-1",
      "sectionId": "chorus-r1-3",
      "text": "Look from here, let wildlife be!",
      "objective": "verbatim",
      "objectReveal": "none"
    },
    {
